WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.637
-Whoo! Let's go!
How you guys doing tonight?

00:00:04.637 --> 00:00:06.673
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:06.673 --> 00:00:08.841
Oh, my God. This has been
a year of firsts for me.

00:00:08.841 --> 00:00:10.643
I moved in with my boyfriend
last year,

00:00:10.643 --> 00:00:12.245
which I didn't think
would happen

00:00:12.245 --> 00:00:13.880
'cause I don't like
to hear men speak.

00:00:13.880 --> 00:00:15.615
[ Laughter ]

00:00:15.615 --> 00:00:17.416
[ Applause ]

00:00:17.416 --> 00:00:20.453
Yeah. I'm hetero, but trust --
it's against my will.

00:00:20.453 --> 00:00:21.621
Um...

00:00:21.621 --> 00:00:23.289
Religious fanatics
say it's a choice.

00:00:23.289 --> 00:00:25.124
I wish it was.

00:00:25.124 --> 00:00:27.493
I would choose women right now.

00:00:27.493 --> 00:00:29.595
Yeah, who doesn't want
to double their wardrobe?

00:00:29.595 --> 00:00:30.630
Are you kidding me?

00:00:30.630 --> 00:00:33.933
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:33.933 --> 00:00:38.170
Yeah, me and my guy got together
March 1st of 2020.

00:00:38.170 --> 00:00:40.473
Yeah. Do that math.

00:00:40.473 --> 00:00:43.209
We went from single
and ready to mingle...

00:00:43.209 --> 00:00:45.445
to married and ready to murder.

00:00:45.445 --> 00:00:47.547
[ Laughter ]

00:00:47.547 --> 00:00:50.616
Yeah, three months in, he looked
me in my eyes and he was like,

00:00:50.616 --> 00:00:53.652
"Joyelle, I love you."

00:00:53.652 --> 00:00:55.655
And I looked him back,
and I said,

00:00:55.655 --> 00:00:58.758
"we need a couples therapist,
stat!"

00:00:58.758 --> 00:01:02.095
I eventually said, "I love you,"
but priorities, you know?

00:01:02.095 --> 00:01:03.329
And people were judging me.

00:01:03.329 --> 00:01:04.830
They were like,
"You just got together.

00:01:04.830 --> 00:01:06.165
Why you need
a couples therapist?"

00:01:06.165 --> 00:01:07.667
I was like,
"Oh, just one little reason.

00:01:07.667 --> 00:01:09.002
It's a tiny reason.

00:01:09.002 --> 00:01:10.736
Uh, we in an
interracial relationship

00:01:10.736 --> 00:01:14.173
during a pandemic race war.
That's all. You know."

00:01:14.173 --> 00:01:17.143
Just the little things.

00:01:17.143 --> 00:01:21.314
And I tell everybody,
get you a couples therapist.

00:01:21.314 --> 00:01:24.817
Okay? It's like hiring a parent
for your relationship.

00:01:24.817 --> 00:01:26.018
[ Laughter ]

00:01:26.018 --> 00:01:28.287
We get into arguments.
I'm like, "You know what?

00:01:28.287 --> 00:01:30.223
We don't even have to
talk about this right now

00:01:30.223 --> 00:01:32.925
because I'm telling on Friday!

00:01:32.925 --> 00:01:35.628
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:35.628 --> 00:01:37.931
At 6:00 p.m."

00:01:37.931 --> 00:01:40.467
[ Laughter ]

00:01:43.836 --> 00:01:46.639
And I wanted somebody, you know,
that could relate to both of us.

00:01:46.639 --> 00:01:48.340
My boyfriend's
half-white, half-Asian.

00:01:48.340 --> 00:01:49.742
I'm Black.

00:01:49.742 --> 00:01:52.612
So I found somebody
that's half-white, half-Black

00:01:52.612 --> 00:01:55.782
so he could relate to both
of us racially, you know?

00:01:55.782 --> 00:01:57.516
And a man,
so he could relate to him

00:01:57.516 --> 00:02:00.119
never feeling a need
to clean the stove.

00:02:00.119 --> 00:02:02.554
[ Laughter ]

00:02:02.554 --> 00:02:05.191
An I have A.D.D., so for,
like, the first two sessions,

00:02:05.191 --> 00:02:07.693
I wasn't even concentrating
'cause I was just trying

00:02:07.693 --> 00:02:10.229
to figure out which one of
his parents was the Black one.

00:02:10.229 --> 00:02:11.764
[ Laughter ]

00:02:11.764 --> 00:02:13.065
Yeah.

00:02:13.065 --> 00:02:15.267
I'm happy to report
I got down to the bottom of it

00:02:15.267 --> 00:02:17.303
because any time one of us
said something sad,

00:02:17.303 --> 00:02:20.273
he'll just be like,
"Mnh-mnh-mnh!"

00:02:20.273 --> 00:02:22.908
[ Laughter ]

00:02:22.908 --> 00:02:25.878
Survey says...Black mama!
That's what that says.

00:02:25.878 --> 00:02:28.981
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:28.981 --> 00:02:31.083
We love him so much.

00:02:31.083 --> 00:02:33.252
He recently had his first baby,
which is great

00:02:33.252 --> 00:02:36.055
if it's anybody
except your couples therapist.

00:02:36.055 --> 00:02:38.358
'Cause homie had the nerve
to take three weeks off.

00:02:38.358 --> 00:02:39.658
What?!

00:02:39.658 --> 00:02:42.928
It's like, "What about
the rest of your kids? Okay?

00:02:42.928 --> 00:02:44.731
Don't nobody care
about this new baby.

00:02:44.731 --> 00:02:47.299
You're just going to leave us
unattended in this apartment

00:02:47.299 --> 00:02:50.035
with all types of cleaning
products, sharp objects,

00:02:50.035 --> 00:02:53.139
and daddy issues lying
around all over the place?!

00:02:53.139 --> 00:02:54.841
You are so selfish."

00:02:54.841 --> 00:02:57.944
And I never thought
I'd ever be able

00:02:57.944 --> 00:02:59.879
to live with
another human being.

00:02:59.879 --> 00:03:02.114
So I was like,
"I need practice," you know?

00:03:02.114 --> 00:03:05.017
So I got a male roommate,
like, 2019.

00:03:05.017 --> 00:03:07.119
'Cause I was like,
"I gotta practice."

00:03:07.119 --> 00:03:10.289
I was working on my nagging
and my passive aggression.

00:03:10.289 --> 00:03:11.757
[ Laughter ]

00:03:11.757 --> 00:03:12.959
Yes. You know.

00:03:12.959 --> 00:03:15.328
So I got a 23-year-old
male roommate.

00:03:15.328 --> 00:03:20.033
So, basically,
I was house-breaking a puppy.

00:03:20.033 --> 00:03:22.235
I rescued him right on time.

00:03:22.235 --> 00:03:25.037
Um, it was like -- I was trying
not to yell at a grown man

00:03:25.037 --> 00:03:27.106
paying rent, but it was like
I was talking to a dog.

00:03:27.106 --> 00:03:29.475
I'm yelling at him like, "Get
down off the couch like that!

00:03:29.475 --> 00:03:32.278
Down, boy!

00:03:32.278 --> 00:03:36.282
Take that chocolate
out of your mouth!

00:03:36.282 --> 00:03:39.085
Did you pee on the floor?!"

00:03:39.085 --> 00:03:41.220
He did.

00:03:41.220 --> 00:03:43.689
The toilet was right there.

00:03:43.689 --> 00:03:46.058
When he peed on the floor,
I rolled up a newspaper,

00:03:46.058 --> 00:03:48.861
and I smacked him on the nose
with it.

00:03:48.861 --> 00:03:51.097
But he's 23.
It just confused him.

00:03:51.097 --> 00:03:53.332
He doesn't know
what a newspaper is.

00:03:53.332 --> 00:03:55.434
[ Laughter ]

00:03:55.434 --> 00:03:58.570
And he was always happy
to see me.

00:03:58.570 --> 00:04:00.773
That annoyed me the most.

00:04:00.773 --> 00:04:02.274
[ Laughter ]

00:04:02.274 --> 00:04:05.410
I would come home just,
you know, mad from the day.

00:04:05.410 --> 00:04:09.782
He'd just be bright-eyed,
wagging his bushy little tail,

00:04:09.782 --> 00:04:13.252
shoving his phone in my face.
Like, "You wanna see this meme?"

00:04:13.252 --> 00:04:15.121
[ Laughter ]

00:04:17.656 --> 00:04:19.758
No.

00:04:19.758 --> 00:04:22.795
I got blue toilet water, boy.
I'm grown!

00:04:22.795 --> 00:04:24.730
[ Laughter ]

00:04:24.730 --> 00:04:26.466
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:27.600 --> 00:04:29.769
I don't want to see a meme.

00:04:29.769 --> 00:04:33.973
I want to see you
stop drinking shower beers.

00:04:33.973 --> 00:04:36.376
I want to see you
buy two-ply toilet paper

00:04:36.376 --> 00:04:38.878
'cause you live with a lady.

00:04:38.878 --> 00:04:41.314
And I want to see you take your
shirt off 'cause he was hot.

00:04:41.314 --> 00:04:43.683
That's the only reason
I let him stay!

00:04:43.683 --> 00:04:46.986
Oh, my God! The Roots!
A moment in Black history.

00:04:46.986 --> 00:04:48.921
Thank you. My name is Joyelle.

